## Summary
In `src/kb_web/templates/workspace_ide.j2.html:1201-1209`:
```javascript
for (const p of toDelete) {
  VFS.deleteFile(p);
  closeTab(p);
  await fetch(`/api/workspaces/${WORKSPACE_ID}/files`, {
    method: "DELETE",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify({ path: p }),
  });
}
```
Meanwhile, the backend endpoint `DELETE /api/workspaces/{workspace_id}/files` in `workspaces.py:909-921` ALREADY handles folder prefixes atomically.

## Impact
Deleting a folder with 50 files fires 50 sequential HTTP requests. If network latency is high or a single request fails, the folder is left in a partially deleted, desynchronized state between the client and server.

## Proposed Fix
Replace the client-side loop with a single atomic deletion call:
```javascript
await fetch(`/api/workspaces/${WORKSPACE_ID}/files`, {
  method: "DELETE",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ path: folderPath }),
});
```
